  <h2>Common request envelope</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">POST /identity.IdentityService/&lt;Method&gt; HTTP/1.1
Host: identity.example.com
Content-Type: application/json
Connect-Protocol-Version: 1
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIs...

{ ...JSON body matching the request proto... }</code></pre>

  <h2>Error format</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-json">{
  "code": "unauthenticated",
  "message": "Invalid or expired access token"
}</code></pre>
  <p>Common Connect error codes: <code>invalid_argument</code>, <code>not_found</code>, <code>already_exists</code>, <code>permission_denied</code>, <code>unauthenticated</code>, <code>resource_exhausted</code> (lockout), <code>internal</code>.</p>

  <h2>Proto source</h2>
  <p>The canonical service definition is in <code>proto/identity/identity.proto</code>. Use <code>buf generate</code> against that file to generate clients in any language.</p>
</DocsLayout>
